Write an implicit cursor program that prompts for a JOB and deletes
the employees working in that JOB. Store the number of records
deleted in a session variable.
(Using Implicit Cursor)
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

sql> ACCEPT P_JOB PROMPT 'Enter Job : '

sql> VARIABLE REC_COUNT NUMBER

sql> DECLARE
BEGIN

   DELETE FROM EMP
   WHERE JOB=UPPER('&P_JOB');

   :REC_COUNT:=SQL%ROWCOUNT;

   DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Rows Deleted = '||SQL%ROWCOUNT);

END;
/

Output:
-------

Enter Job : CLERK

Rows Deleted = 4

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.

Check Session Variable:
-----------------------

sql> PRINT REC_COUNT;

Output:
-------

REC_COUNT
---------
4


