 9
Write a Parameter Cursor program that promotes CLERK who earn
more than 1000 to SR CLERK and increases the salary by 10%.
Pass CLERK as a parameter to the Cursor.
Use Parameter Cursor, FOR LOOP and FOR UPDATE clause.
====================================================================

SQL Command:
------------

sql> SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;

sql> DECLARE

CURSOR C1(P_JOB VARCHAR2) IS
SELECT EMPNO,ENAME,JOB,SAL
FROM EMP
WHERE JOB=P_JOB
AND SAL>1000
FOR UPDATE;

BEGIN

FOR R IN C1('CLERK')
LOOP

UPDATE EMP
SET JOB='SR CLERK',
    SAL=SAL*1.10
WHERE CURRENT OF C1;

DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE
(R.ENAME||' Promoted Successfully');

END LOOP;

COMMIT;

END;
/

Output:
-------

ADAMS Promoted Successfully
MILLER Promoted Successfully

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


Verify:
-------

sql> SELECT EMPNO,ENAME,JOB,SAL
FROM EMP
WHERE JOB='SR CLERK';

Output:
-------

EMPNO  ENAME    JOB        SAL
-----  -------  ---------  ----
7876   ADAMS    SR CLERK   1210
7934   MILLER   SR CLERK   1430


